WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.660
Part three: your shifts, your point person, and reminders.

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:09.308
Your shifts lists everyone in your family: who, where, and when.

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:15.973
Each one shows the point person running that station. Their number shows up 48 hours before your shift.

00:00:16.173 --> 00:00:22.880
Can't make it? Tap Cancel, up to 48 hours before. After that, email the coordinators.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:36.030
Inside those 48 hours, Call and Text buttons show up. Running late, or lost? Call or text your point person. The text starts with your name and your shift, so they know who it is.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:43.440
Homeroom guides see which guard they're assigned to, right on the shift, once their coordinator picks it.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:50.669
Put your family's shifts on your phone's calendar. Subscribe once, and it updates itself if a shift changes.

00:00:50.869 --> 00:00:53.857
Use this button on an iPhone, Mac or Outlook,

00:00:54.057 --> 00:01:00.150
or this one for Google Calendar. Reminders come the day before, and two hours before.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.030
Next, in part four: what your family owes, background checks, and adding family members.
